Every commitment consumes time and attention. Saying yes to a meaningful goal often requires postponing or declining lower-value activities.

Action: Identify one distraction or commitment you can reduce this week.

## 3. Six productivity myths the book challenges

The authors explain that several popular beliefs can prevent meaningful progress.&#x20;

[image](https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=https://www.summary.com\&sz=32)

Key Ideas and Takeaways

+1



| Common belief                                    | A more useful perspective                                            |
| ------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Everything matters equally.                      | Some actions have far greater impact.                                |
| Multitasking makes you efficient.                | Switching between demanding tasks can reduce focus.                  |
| Discipline must be constant.                     | Use discipline to establish helpful routines.                        |
| Willpower is always available.                   | Schedule difficult work when your energy is high.                    |
| A balanced life means equal time for everything. | Give priorities the attention they need while protecting essentials. |
| Big success requires doing everything.           | Start with the highest-impact next action.                           |

