## 5. A simple daily routine

Morning — 5 minutes

Decide your ONE Thing and write down what completing it will accomplish.

Focus session — 60–90 minutes

Work on that priority. Silence notifications and avoid switching tasks.

Evening — 5 minutes

Review your progress, identify what distracted you, and choose tomorrow's priority.

## 6. The biggest takeaways

- Focus is a choice; protect it deliberately.
- Being busy is not the same as making progress.
- Small, consistent actions compound when performed in the right order.
- Schedule important work instead of hoping you'll find time.
- Your priorities should guide your calendar, not the other way around.
- Ambition matters, but health and relationships need protection too.

## Final lesson

The book isn't asking you to do only one thing for the rest of your life. It asks you to identify the most important thing at the current stage, complete it, and then move to the next meaningful step.

Remember: You don't need to win every battle today. You need to make the move that makes tomorrow's progress easier.&#x20;

